From 315d081ad87064514b870beaa4d45513bb5e9d88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 10:18:32 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(adaptive): read the bore's star cell through offset
 rounding noise

The Z 15 and Z 5 levels of the user's bore hand the planner a
328-vertex disc outline. Its opening at the corner radius kept edges
one or two Clipper units long (1.4e-6 mm) that turn back about the
pole. The star law read each as a shadow, and the kernel test read its
line as a wall through the area. The star cell was refused, and the
growth rings cut those levels in 999.92 mm of feed against 334.31 mm.

Star::new now drops the vertices of an opened row loop that stand
within 1e-5 mm of the last vertex kept. Each bore level takes the morph
spiral: Z 15 and Z 5 cut 330.07 mm and reach the wall in -Y. The bore
pin moves to (1642, 1614, 300), measured on macOS arm64 in release.

Fixes #4010

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
